# GATE 0 READINESS (launch day, 2026-07-30). s1_entry_met is the gate that admits real capital,
# and NOTHING assembled its evidence dict from reality -- so "what is actually left?" required
# reading five subsystems by hand. This measures every criterion against its proving artifact and
# splits DESK-owed from PRINCIPAL-owed, which is the only distinction that matters on launch day.
# An unmeasurable criterion reads BLOCKED-UNKNOWN, never READY: a gate that counts "could not
# measure" as satisfied is how capital gets admitted it should not.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_gate0_ready.py -> data/gate0_readiness.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
9 */4 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_gate0_ready.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/gate0_readiness.log 2>&1

# GENERATION DIVERSITY (HYPOTHESIS_MAX #2/#3/#6, unblocked at Gate 0 entry 2026-07-30). The spec
# deferred the collapse detector with an explicit trigger -- "build it when generation cadence
# upgrades to weekly at S1/Gate-0 entry" -- because generation was low-volume and the failure mode
# was unreachable. That trigger fires today.
# WHAT IT MEASURES that nothing else could: novel_rate, the share of generated ideas that were
# genuinely NEW questions rather than reparameterisations. "420 candidates tested" and "one
# question asked 420 ways" are identical from a count, and 420/0 is precisely the record that
# needed telling apart. Plus mechanism entropy (normalised by ITEM count, so 2 fingerprints across
# 50 ideas reads ~0.18 rather than a perfect 1.0), market breadth counting cross-sectional
# universes properly, and cross-generator herding between seats.
# The detector NEVER blocks generation -- instrumentation that pages the weekly panel, per spec.
# EVIDENCE: libs/research/{collapse_detector,variation_blocker,mechanism_fingerprint}.py;
#           tests/research/test_{collapse_detector,variation_blocker}.py (37 tests)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
23 9 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/run_generation_diversity.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/gen_diversity.log 2>&1

# SAFETY DRILLS (GAP_REGISTER row #2 Gate-0 item (c): "monthly host-death and ladder DRILLS have
# never been run"). staging.s2_entry_met reads `critical_drill_failures`, and that field defaults
# to the REFUSING sentinel because no code had ever produced a drill record -- so the S2 gate was
# correctly closed and had no way to open.
# WHY DRILLS AND NOT UNIT TESTS: a unit test asks "does this function return the right value?"; a
# drill asks "does the INVARIANT survive the event it exists for?" -- process death mid-position,
# a pager unanswered for four hours, a clock moving backwards. Those cross function boundaries and
# PERSISTED STATE, which is where the crash-loop-resets-the-timer class of bug lives.
# NO DRILL PLACES OR CANCELS A LIVE ORDER: pure decision functions against temp-directory copies
# of state. A drill that could move money would be a larger risk than the one it certifies.
# Weekly rather than the monthly the register asked for -- the cost is seconds.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_drills.py -> data/drill_report.json + data/drill_log.jsonl;
#           tests/ops/test_drills.py breaks each rail and proves the drill catches it
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
40 3 * * 1 cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/run_drills.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/drills.log 2>&1
